+# Explicit-only RPC UI interactions (compatibility candidate)
+
+This additive contract is effective for rpc-ui before extension initialization.
+It does not change ordinary TUI defaults or write a global setting.
+
+`--rpc-preflight` returns `get_compatibility.data.rpcUiInteractionPolicy` without
+loading the ordinary CLI, configuration, extensions or Session runtime. Verify
+that report and drain/reap the probe before starting a UI worker. The ordinary
+worker's first `ready.interactionPolicy` repeats the immutable effective policy:
+
+```json
+{"version":"1","explicitAnswersOnly":true,"nativeExpiry":"cancel","toolExpiry":"cancel","invalidAnswer":"pending"}
+```
+
+`negotiate_protocol`, `get_interaction_policy` and `respond_ui` bypass the serial command queue,
+including during extension startup. A pending root question remains pending
+while protocol v2 is negotiated and acknowledged. Process startup budgets do not
+include the human wait. `get_state` may still wait for extension initialization.
+
+```json
+{"id":"p","type":"get_interaction_policy"}
+{"id":"a","type":"respond_ui","targetId":"native-ui-id","answer":{"type":"value","value":"exact option label"}}
+```
+
+Other answer variants are `{type:"confirm",confirmed:boolean}`,
+`{type:"cancel",timedOut?:boolean}` and `{type:"ask",answers:[{id,selectedOptions,customInput?}]}`.
+The successful response data is `{status:"answered"|"cancelled"|"expired"|"invalid"|"stale"}`.
+Malformed command schemas fail with `INVALID_UI_COMMAND`. Business-invalid
+answers keep the request and its original deadline pending. Exact question IDs,
+order, labels, types, cardinality and duplicate options are validated before an
+answer can win. `confirmed:false` is an explicit answer; cancellation is separate.
+
+The first valid answer, cancellation, signal abort or expiry removes a pending
+request once. A deadline check runs before accepting a reply even when the timer
+callback is delayed. Native ask expiry and `timedOut:true` cancel; no recommended
+option is generated. The legacy `extension_ui_response` side channel has the
+same settlement rules, but does not acknowledge consumption. Prefer `respond_ui`.
+Native cancellation notifications carry `targetId` and an optional reason
+`cancelled`, `expired` or `aborted`. Tool and URI response ID families stay separate.
+
+The builtin HTML ask tool receives `explicitAnswersOnly` through the real RPC UI
+and core ToolContextStore/user-wait wrappers. One original monotonic form budget
+bounds all fields, retries, input and editor prompts. The same-process extension
+option `deadlineMonotonicMs` carries that budget through wrappers; it is never a
+browser wire timestamp. RPC requests advertise remaining `timeout` milliseconds.
+The parser, native timer and abort paths cannot turn silence or cancellation into
+preselected form data. A timed-out formDialog result also cancels.
+
+The public TypeScript RpcClient exposes `interactionPolicy`,
+`onExtensionUIRequest`, `getInteractionPolicy` and `respondUI`. Register the UI
+listener before `start()`; a startup listener can validate the cached ready policy
+and answer while `start()` is still awaiting negotiation. Generated Python, Go,
+Rust and TypeScript wire clients share the authored schema and tagged answer union.
+
+Host policy remains separate: its default target is 30 minutes from creating the
+pending record, configurable for later requests and bounded by earlier native
+constraints. Redelivery, browser refresh and disconnect never renew a request.
+Host expiry cancels and requests Stop. Worker replacement cannot restore old UI
+IDs or replay an answer. The S0 browser fixture does not grant product Session access.
